317 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 158 0 R
/E (A 6T SRAM cell is the most commonly used SRAM memory cell structure because it provides a good balance between speed, stability, and power consumption. The term 6T means that the cell is constructed using six MOS transistors: two PMOS transistors and four NMOS transistors implemented using CMOS technology)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
318 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 158 0 R
/E (.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
