/P 158 0 R
/E <>
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
320 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 158 0 R
/E (Two additional NMOS transistors act as access transistors. These access transistors connect the internal storage nodes to the two bit lines, namely BL \(Bit Line\) and BLB \(Bit Line Bar\). The gates of both access transistors are connected to a common control line called the word line \(WL\). When the word line is enabled, the access transistors turn ON and allow data transfer between the cell and the bit lines.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
321 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 158 0 R
/E (The six transistors in a 6T SRAM cell are divided as follows:)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
