/E (In hold operation, the SRAM cell retains its stored data without any external access.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
357 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 160 0 R
/E (When the word line \(WL\) is disabled, the access transistors are turned OFF, isolating the cell from the bit lines. The cross-coupled inverters continue to reinforce each other through positive feedback, maintaining the stored logic value.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
358 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 160 0 R
/E (Since no switching activity occurs during hold mode, it ideally consumes very low dynamic power. However, leakage currents may still be present, especially in deep submicron technologies.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
359 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 160 0 R
/E (The ability of the SRAM cell to maintain data reliably during hold mode is determined by its static noise margin \(SNM\).)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
