362 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 160 0 R
/E (SNM is the maximum noise voltage that an SRAM cell can tolerate without changing its stored data. It indicates the stability of the cell during hold, read, and write operations. Higher SNM means better reliability and stronger resistance to noise.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
