547 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 170 0 R
/E (The stacking effect is a leakage reduction technique used in CMOS circuits by connecting two or more transistors in series and turning them OFF simultaneously as shown in the Fig4.4. This reduces leakage current because the voltage across each transistor becomes lower.)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
548 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 170 0 R
/E (In the 6T SRAM cell, stacking is implemented by adding series transistors in the pull-down or access path. When these transistors are OFF, subthreshold leakage current decreases due to reduced gate-to-source voltage.)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
