/E (A conventional 6T SRAM cell as shown in Fig:4.7 suffers from leakage power dissipation during standby mode. To reduce this, a Header with Footer power-gating technique is used, where a PMOS header transistor is connected between VDD and the SRAM cell, and an NMOS footer transistor is placed between the cell and ground. These sleep transistors reduce leakage current and improve power efficiency.)
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
