/Title (The results show a comparison of SRAM performance under normal, header, footer, and combined power gating conditions. It is observed that the Hold SNM is highest in the Header+Footer configuration, indicating improved stability in standby mode. Read SNM decreases in power-gated designs due to added circuit complexity and voltage drops. Write SNM improves in optimized designs, showing better writability of the cell. Read delay is reduced in header and combined configurations, enhancing read speed. Write delay is also minimized in the Header+Footer case, indicating faster switching. Power consumption is reduced in certain configurations, especially in read operation with combined techniques. Overall, the results demonstrate a trade-off between stability, speed, and power, with the Header+Footer configuration providing the best overall performance.)
/Dest [38 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 794 0 R
/Next 1285 0 R
>>
