1283 0 obj
<<
/Title (The performance of the 6T SRAM cell is evaluated based on key parameters such as SNM, delay, and power consumption obtained from Cadence simulations. The results indicate that the SRAM cell exhibits high stability during hold condition, while read and write operations show comparatively lower SNM due to operational disturbances.)
/Dest [38 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1103 0 R
/Next 1284 0 R
>>
endobj
1284 0 obj
<<
/Title (Delay analysis shows that the SRAM cell performs fast read and write operations, although a slight increase in delay is observed when power reduction techniques such as stacking and power gating are applied. This is due to the additional resistance introduced in the current path. Power analysis demonstrates that leakage power is significantly reduced using stacking effect and power gating techniques. The implementation of these techniques improves overall energy efficiency, especially during standby mode.)
/Dest [38 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1103 0 R
/Prev 1283 0 R
>>
endobj
