1674 0 obj
<<
/Title (The Static Noise Margin \(SNM\) of the 6T SRAM cell is evaluated using Cadence simulations to analyze the stability of the cell under different operating conditions. SNM is obtained from the butterfly curve generated using DC analysis of the cross-coupled inverters. Separate analyses are carried out for hold, read, and write conditions to understand the variation in stability. The side length of the maximum square that can be fitted inside the butterfly curve represents the SNM value as shown in Fig 5.1.)
/Dest [34 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1667 0 R
/Next 1675 0 R
>>
endobj
